# Group Objects by Key

```javascript
function groupBy(arr, key) {
  return arr.reduce((acc, obj) => {
    const groupKey = obj[key];
    (acc[groupKey] = acc[groupKey] || []).push(obj);
    return acc;
  }, {});
}
```

**Usage:**

```javascript
const users = [
  { name: 'Alice', role: 'admin' },
  { name: 'Bob', role: 'user' },
  { name: 'Carol', role: 'admin' },
];

console.log(groupBy(users, 'role'));
// {
//   admin: [{ name: 'Alice', ... }, { name: 'Carol', ... }],
//   user:  [{ name: 'Bob', ... }]
// }
```

**Variant: support a custom key function** (e.g., group by computed values like dates or nested properties):

```javascript
function groupBy(arr, getKey) {
  return arr.reduce((acc, obj) => {
    const groupKey = typeof getKey === 'function' ? getKey(obj) : obj[getKey];
    (acc[groupKey] = acc[groupKey] || []).push(obj);
    return acc;
  }, {});
}

// Example: group by first letter of name
groupBy(users, u => u.name[0]);
```

**TypeScript version:**

```typescript
function groupBy<T>(arr: T[], getKey: string | ((item: T) => string)): Record<string, T[]> {
  return arr.reduce<Record<string, T[]>>((acc, obj) => {
    const groupKey = typeof getKey === 'function' ? getKey(obj) : (obj as any)[getKey];
    (acc[groupKey] = acc[groupKey] || []).push(obj);
    return acc;
  }, {});
}
```

**Notes:**
- Uses `Object.prototype` safely — no mutation of the original array.
- Keys are coerced to strings (so `1` and `'1'` group together).
- If you're targeting modern environments, `Object.groupBy(arr, fn)` is now built into JavaScript (ES2024).

# Group Array of Objects by Key

## Basic Solution

```javascript
function groupBy(arr, key) {
  return arr.reduce((result, item) => {
    const group = item[key];
    (result[group] ||= []).push(item);
    return result;
  }, {});
}
```

## Usage Example

```javascript
const users = [
  { name: "Alice", age: 25, city: "NYC" },
  { name: "Bob", age: 30, city: "LA" },
  { name: "Carol", age: 25, city: "NYC" },
];

console.log(groupBy(users, "city"));
// {
//   NYC: [ { name: "Alice", ... }, { name: "Carol", ... } ],
//   LA:  [ { name: "Bob", ... } ]
// }
```

## More Flexible Version (supports function keys)

```javascript
function groupBy(arr, keyFn) {
  const getKey = typeof keyFn === "function" ? keyFn : (item) => item[keyFn];
  return arr.reduce((result, item) => {
    const group = getKey(item);
    (result[group] ||= []).push(item);
    return result;
  }, {});
}

// Group by computed property
groupBy(users, (u) => u.age >= 30 ? "senior" : "junior");
```

## Built-in Alternative (modern browsers)

```javascript
Object.groupBy(users, (u) => u.city);
